{
  "title": "103: al-Asr العصر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالْعَصْرِۙ‏(1)\nWAL A’SRE.\nBy the Time!\nاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَفِىْ خُسْرٍۙ‏(2)\nINNAL INSAANA LAFEE KHUSRIN.\nVerily, man is in loss!\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالْحَقِّ   ۙ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالصَّبْرِ‏(3)\nILLAL LAZEENA AAMAANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA TAWAASAW BIL HAQQE WA TAWAASAW BISSABR.\nSave those who believe, and do good deeds, and exhort each other to truth and exhort each other to endurance",
  "merits": "There are 3 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the person who recites this Surah in his recommended prayers will have a shining face on the Day of Judgement.\nThe one who recites this Surah will be patient in adversity and will be counted from among the people of truth. If this Surah is written after Isha prayers and kept, it will be a safety from the tyrant ruler in whose presence one is brought."
}
